            <ArticleTitle>Coagulopathy presenting as calf pain in a racquetball player.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>390-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Most cases of lower leg pain in athletes result from musculoskeletal injury. Occasionally these patients do not respond to treatment in a timely fashion. This should alert the clinician to rethink the original diagnosis and consider more unusual causes of leg pain. Deep venous thrombosis must be considered in a young athletic person experiencing unexplained persistent calf pain after exercise. Further investigation may be necessary to rule out a hereditary or acquired hypercoagulable state.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
